{
  "title": "Rendered decision header says [Decision 0] on every decision of every game",
  "description": "build_pilot_decision hardcoded index=0 (pilot_bridge.py, the \
`decision = Decision(index=0, snapshot_index=0, ...)` literal), and that field is what \
decision_renderer.py renders as the leading `[Decision N, snapshot=M] Turn T PHASE - \
player`. So N never moved. Measured by karn-ranokau-stable across 400 run-2 rollouts: \
29,906 of 29,906 decisions rendered as Decision 0. CONFIRMED on lascar against the \
pinned master (e4f9d1a4) rather than assumed -- it is not a v2-agent-loop-only path, \
the literal is in the shared pilot bridge, so every pilot path is affected. Committed \
test fixtures show it too: pipelines/synth/test_engine_shim.py has [Decision 0, \
snapshot=0] on turns 1, 2 and 3 in four separate fixtures, which is the defect baked \
into expected output. CONSEQUENCE: the header exists to tell the model where it is in \
the game and it told it nothing, so the model could not distinguish its first decision \
from its fortieth; and the card-text work about to measure 'how far back was this card \
revealed' would have been reading a position field with no position in it. FIXED on \
branch fix/decision-index: the index is threaded from a counter on PilotLoopState \
(decisions_seen), advanced only for results carrying action_pending -- asked of the \
DATA rather than inferred from 'the rendered text differs from the input', which is \
true today only by coincidence of how the renderer early-returns. snapshot_index stays \
0 deliberately: the pilot renders one snapshot per decision, so there 0 is the true \
value rather than a missing one. HARNESS_EPOCH 62 -> 63, because every prompt from the \
second decision onward now differs in header text; prompts collected before and after \
are not comparable. Prompt goldens regenerated. Negative control: restoring index=0 \
fails the new header test and leaves the non-decision test passing. FOLDED IN 2026-08-24: ranokau filed the same defect independently as p2-decision-header-counter-never-increments (deleted with this update, its content kept here). Their measurement, over 400 recorded rollout trajectories -- 20 GRPO steps x 20 games, Boros mirror: 29,906 rendered decisions, decision number 0 in all 29,906. Their consequence note is worth keeping verbatim in substance: trajectories there run to a median of 76 decisions and a max of 110, against a context window that keeps 40 at full fidelity and summarises 20 more, so a policy is routinely reasoning about a position it cannot locate. ONE CORRECTION TO THAT REPORT, measured rather than argued: it says the snapshot field does vary, so only the counter was frozen. In the PILOT path it does not. Over 8,190 headers in real llm_trace files on lascar, decision index is 0 in 8,190 of 8,190 AND snapshot is 0 in 8,190 of 8,190. Both were literals in the same constructor, which is what the code says. The varying snapshot values visible in goldens come from the analysis/export path, which builds Decision from exported data carrying real snapshot indices -- a different producer, and the likely source of the impression. STILL OPEN and deliberately not fixed: snapshot_index remains a hardcoded 0 in the pilot path. Whether 0 is correct there or a second frozen literal is untested, and it should be established before anyone either fixes it or documents it as intended. FIXED AT 36f02d3d.",
